            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "hunterman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very runny and very sweet, needs some kind of thickener like a couple tablespoons of cornstarch.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-26T11:23:22.237Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lbolea"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This pie was tasty, but it never set up in the middle. I baked it 15 minutes longer than the recipe said and it just never firmed up. I took it out of the oven because I was afraid the top would burn. I even refrigerated it after cooling and it never solidified. I will not make this again.",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-19T13:05:01.990Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kendra"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good flavor. It was a nice change from the normal pudding and cream cheese peanut butter pies. I may have underbaked mine though because it was still pretty soft in the middle even after it completely cooled although I baked it 10 minutes longer than stated.",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-16T06:34:01.787Z"
